  "question": {
    "text": "Between the following two statements:\nStatement I : Let $\\vec{a}=\\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-3 \\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b}=2 \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}-\\hat{k}$. Then the vector $\\vec{r}$ satisfying $\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{r}=\\vec{a} \\times \\vec{b}$ and $\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{r}=0$ is of magnitude $\\sqrt{10}$.<br />Statement II : In a triangle $A B C, \\cos 2 A+\\cos 2 B+\\cos 2 C \\geq-\\frac{3}{2}$."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\bar{a}=\\hat{i}+2 \\hat{j}-3 \\hat{k} \\\\ & \\bar{a}=2 \\hat{i}+\\hat{j}-\\hat{k} \\\\ & \\bar{a} \\times \\bar{r}=\\bar{a} \\times \\bar{b} ; \\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{r}=0 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\bar{a} \\times(\\bar{r}-\\bar{b})=\\overline{0} \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\bar{a}=\\lambda(\\bar{r}-\\bar{b}) \\\\ & \\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{a}=\\lambda(\\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{r}-\\bar{a} \\cdot \\bar{b}) \\\\ & 14=-7 \\lambda \\Rightarrow \\lambda=-2 \\\\ & \\frac{-\\bar{a}}{2}=\\bar{r}-\\bar{b} \\Rightarrow \\bar{r}=\\bar{b}-\\frac{\\bar{a}}{2} \\\\ & =\\frac{2 \\bar{b}-\\bar{a}}{2}=\\frac{3 \\hat{i}+\\hat{k}}{2}\\end{aligned}$<br />Statement (I) is incorrect\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\cos 2 \\mathrm{~A}+\\cos 2 \\mathrm{~B}+\\cos 2 \\mathrm{c} \\geq-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n& 2 \\mathrm{~A}+2 \\mathrm{~B}+2 \\mathrm{C}=2 \\pi \\\\\n& \\cos 2 \\mathrm{~A}+\\cos 2 \\mathrm{~B}+\\cos 2 \\mathrm{C} \\\\\n& =-1-4 \\cos \\mathrm{A} \\cdot \\cos \\mathrm{B} \\cdot \\cos \\mathrm{C} \\\\\n& \\geq-1-4 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& =-\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Statement (II) is correct."
  }
